  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 130 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nBreezy WNW winds prevailed this afternoon in the wake of yesterday's \nstorm system while clear conditions developed across the area. Winds \nwill diminish tonight while a progressive shortwave trough emerges \nfrom the Rockies during the early morning hours on Thu. It is a \ncompact system that will bring some shower activity to parts of \nsouthern Kansas on Thursday. Rainfall amounts are expected to remain \nlight. Increasing clouds can be expected as we move through the \novernight hours which could keep minimum temperatures slightly \nhigher over parts of southern KS. Clouds and shower activity along \nwith some weak low-level cold air advection in the wake of the \nfrontal boundary will bring cooler conditions to the area on Thu \nwith highs mostly in the 50s.\n\nThis progressive system will exit the area Thursday night with \nclearing conditions anticipated. Shortwave ridging will arrive in \nit's wake while persisting into early next week resulting in mild \nand dry weather conditions. Above average temperatures will return \nby Sunday and persist through the middle of the week.",
